@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@ A first-person Pac-Man clone for Roblox, built with Rojo, strict Luau, and Lune
 
 **Non-negotiable:** no code without a tracker issue, and work is done only when its `check.sh` passes. **Every change is made in a git worktree under `.worktree/` and lands by pull request** (a capture lands with `./zn land`, after a local full gate); the main checkout is never edited, except by `./zn` itself (`ready`, `stop`, `sync`, and the board refresh after every publish or `land`), which only fast-forwards it, clears ignored files from item folders that left it, and writes ignored files (`prompt.md`, `.cache/board.html`, the dispatcher's run state in `.cache/dispatch/`) (zz-rules skill, Worktrees and Landing a change). Start execution with `/z-run <R-id>` in a session in the main checkout: that is z-work with that raft named (`./zn work <R-id>`). With no raft named, run `./zn work`. The unattended launcher stays `./zn dispatch <id>` (zz-rules skill, Dispatch; `.models.toml` names the models). Before doing anything, read the skill that applies. The skills hold all the rules.
 
-**Design approval:** a human approves every design with `./zn approve <id>`, run in their own terminal in the prep worktree; it is refused in any agent session. Tell the user to run it; never try to (zz-rules skill, the approve row).
+**Design approval:** a human approves every design with `./zn approve <id>`, run in their own terminal, from anywhere in the checkout (it finds the design, records the approval and publishes it); it is refused in any agent session. Tell the user to run it; never try to (zz-rules skill, the approve row).
 
 **Subagents:** don't use `fork` subagents. Delegate to a plain subagent (general-purpose) with `model: "sonnet"` and a full brief. The exceptions are design and code reviewers, which the skills pin to Opus 5.5.
 
